.TH PIDOF 1 2026-10-27 procps-ng
.SH NAME
pidof \- find the process ID of a running program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY pidof
.RB [ \-cqstwx ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR omit-pid [\c
.BR , .\|.\|.\&]]
.RB [ \-S
.IR separator ]
.I program
\&.\|.\|.
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Pidof
reports the identifiers
of processes
.RI ( pid s)
with names matching
.I program
to the standard output stream.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \fB\-c\fP
Report only pids using the same root directory as
.BR pidof .
Ignored for non-root users,
who are unable to determine the root directory of processes
they do not own.
.IP "\fB-o\fP \fIomit-pid\fP[\fB,\fP.\|.\|.]"
Do not report pids matching any
.I omit-pid.
.B Pidof
interprets an
.I omit-pid
of
.B %PPID
as its parent process,
in other words the calling shell or shell script.
Specify multiple
.I omit-pids
by separating them with commas in the option argument.
Specifying
.B \-o
more than once supplements the list of
.I omit-pids.
.IP \fB\-q\fP
Operate quietly,
suppressing output.
See \[lq]EXIT STATUS\[rq] below.
.IP \fB\-s\fP
Report only a single matching pid.
.IP "\fB\-S\fP \fIseparator\fP"
Use \fIseparator\fP as a separator put between pids.
Used only when more than one pids are printed for the program.
If \fIseparator\fR is \[aq]\[aq] then pids are separated
by the null byte \fI\[aq]\[rs]0\[aq]\fR.
The \fB\-d\fR option is an alias for this option for sysvinit
.B pidof
compatibility.
.IP \fB\-t\fP
Report thread identifiers instead of pids.
.IP \fB\-w\fP
Report processes that lack a visible command line,
such as kernel worker threads.
.IP \fB\-x\fP
Report pids of shells running scripts named
.I program.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
At least one program was found with the requested name.
.TP
.B 1
No program was found with the requested name.
.SH BUGS
When using the \fB\-x\fP option,
.B pidof
only has a simple method for detecting scripts and will miss scripts that,
for example, use env. This limitation is due to how the scripts look in
the proc filesystem.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pgrep (1),
.BR pkill (1)
.SH AUTHOR
.MT jcapik@redhat.com
Jaromir Capik
.ME
